  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence is\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=r\\cdot f(n).\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we must determine the common ratio $r$ and state the first term $f(1).$ The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {8}^{1}=\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 8=6, \\\\ f(2) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {8}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 64=48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{48}{6}=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula for the geometric sequence is\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=8f(n),\\,f(1)=6,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$",
